/ ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/ `lazy` / `collect` basics.
/
/ Run from the repo root:
/   cargo run -- examples/lazy_and_collect.qpl
/ ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/ `lazy` as the first token stores the query PLAN under a name, not a table.
/ Nothing touches the file yet.
t: lazy load `examples/data/trades.parquet

/ Extend the plan by re-assigning the binding. Still lazy, still no execution.
t: select sym, side, price, size from t where size > 100
t: update notional: price * size from t

/ Reading a lazy binding without collecting just prints its (optimised) plan.
select from t

/ `collect` runs the plan once and binds the result as a normal in-memory table.
tm: collect t
select sym, notional from tm where side = `buy

/ `cols` always resolves to a table, even on a lazy binding.
cols t
